{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories","id":157997,"title":"[Rough idea for an Exigent] The Chosen of Stories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T10:22:05-07:00","id":157997,"title":"[Rough idea for an Exigent] The Chosen of Stories","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So I had the seed of this idea recently on these forums while discussing the Orphan's Tales, by Catherynne Valente. It's germinated in some odd directions and started off tangential at best. But the idea started there, and I feel like it's important to acknowledge one's sources.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">That said, I had a thought for a charm tree where the vast majority of charms don't have prerequisites in Abilities or Attributes or Virtues, but in something a little less tangible: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Stories.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ideally, the endpoint of this Exigent (who likely springs from Talespinner, but could come from anywhere) is someone containing dozens of stories: tragedies, comedies, adventures, horrors, romances, patently untrue legends...and drew strength from them, channeled them, and did their damnedest to make them--or at least the lessons learned--real in some sense even if they never were.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Occasionally, I'm tossing out examples of real-world stories below, but obviously these don't apply to Creation. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This would probably need to go to a player who wants to write these herself, even if IC they're getting learned by the character externally.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is just the rough shape of an idea. I intend to revisit it <i>at least</i> once 3e drops, and probably more heavily come the release of the Exigent hardback.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Random thoughts follow, more to come as I figure out how to frame them:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Keyword: Library</b> -- The Exalt is intended to learn multiple iterations of this charm, and finds that subsequent iterations come more easily. After the first purchase, the cost is reduced. Soul-Sustaining Saga is the most likely candidate, but this may pop up in more places.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Soul-Sustaining Saga</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Develop a Principle based on a story. As long as you retain this intimacy, you gain an extra willpower per night of rest. More potent intimacies may grant more WP or other benefits. This charm may be repurchased any number of times for a greatly reduced price; only the most potent intimacy provides the WP bonuses. This forms the basis for most future charms. The intensity of the Intimacy may be a secondary prerequisite for later charms.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <br /> <b>Sharing Campfire Songs</b><br /> The Exalt tells the story and share the intimacy he possesses towards it at minor levels. At higher levels this Intimacy spreads beyond the immediate audience and spreads through a town or city.<br /> <br /> <b>Life Imitates Art</b><br /> By drawing parallels between one of her stories and the current situation, the Exalt subtly influences people to continue to act in a befitting manner.<br /> <br /> <b>Heroic Icon Memento</b><br /> The Exalt takes on a visible trapping of a particular character in the story (e.g. the shaving-dish helm of Don Quixote or the Lionskin of Hercules), and gains an appropriate specialty (or other appropriate benefit) as long as it is openly displayed. Does not stack. <br /> <br /> <b>In Gilded Memories</b><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Exalt creates stories from her own past for Soul-Sustaining Saga. In doing so, she codifies it and elides any details that contradict the core meaning she creates for it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Everyone Loves A Story</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Exalt can treat story-based initimacies he's shared as positive intimacies toward himself.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:36:54-07:00","id":158028,"title":"","content":"This is a very cool idea. Are the Story Exalted meant to commentate on Raksha (and other Fair Folk) in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:52:03-07:00","id":158042,"title":"","content":"They're certainly not <i>intended</i> to. But the end result is almost inherently going to bear some similarities. I strongly imagine that somewhere along the line they end up conjuring the phantoms of their stories, and it's not deliberately supposed to resemble Fair Folk shaping, but I don't see a way you can do it without at least wading in those waters. If I thought there was going to be something like Shaping Combat, there would definitely be capabilities along those lines. But that, mercifully, sounds like it's going to be gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:15:37-07:00","id":158053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158042#post158042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're certainly not <i>intended</i> to. But the end result is almost inherently going to bear some similarities. I strongly imagine that somewhere along the line they end up conjuring the phantoms of their stories, and it's not deliberately supposed to resemble Fair Folk shaping, but I don't see a way you can do it without at least wading in those waters. If I thought there was going to be something like Shaping Combat, there would definitely be capabilities along those lines. But that, mercifully, sounds like it's going to be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead, what you might allow is the creation of storyscapes. And then maybe later powers where Attributes and Abilities gain extra functions that they normally wouldn't have, like fighting someone's piercing gaze with Investigation or doing physical damage with Performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:34:41-07:00","id":158072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158053#post158053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, what you might allow is the creation of storyscapes. And then maybe later powers where Attributes and Abilities gain extra functions that they normally wouldn't have, like fighting someone's piercing gaze with Investigation or doing physical damage with Performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...do not know if this is a direction I desire to go. The overt enhancements to the actual Exalt should <i>seem </i>minimal. The Exigent has a preternatural sense of when you're talking about her, frequently turning up right when you need her--and could summon (see above disclaimers re: characters mentioned) the Little Mermaid to fetch a lost treasure in the ocean, or the Giant Mouse of Minsk to terrify and scatter her foes. She reminds you that you're a great hero, and that you fought off a horde of hobgoblins singlehandedly and bravely; in the back of your mind you thought it wasn't quite like that at all--wasn't it a single misshapen and mad Wyld mutant?--but by the gods! If she believes in you like that she must be right.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure how far and how deep and how powerful the charms get. But the storyscape is already something theoretically possible. The others, I'm less sure about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:31:56-07:00","id":158104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158072#post158072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I...do not know if this is a direction I desire to go. The overt enhancements to the actual Exalt should <i>seem </i>minimal. The Exigent has a preternatural sense of when you're talking about her, frequently turning up right when you need her--and could summon (see above disclaimers re: characters mentioned) the Little Mermaid to fetch a lost treasure in the ocean, or the Giant Mouse of Minsk to terrify and scatter her foes. She reminds you that you're a great hero, and that you fought off a horde of hobgoblins singlehandedly and bravely; in the back of your mind you thought it wasn't quite like that at all--wasn't it a single misshapen and mad Wyld mutant?--but by the gods! If she believes in you like that she must be right.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure how far and how deep and how powerful the charms get. But the storyscape is already something theoretically possible. The others, I'm less sure about.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> So, then! How would you structure Charms? Would each genre have an associated Trait of some kind, something like Astrological Colleges? Or would these Attribute based Exalted? Or something stranger, where, if you want to use Investigator genre Charms, you have have an Intelligence + Investigation of a certain amount?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:23:00-07:00","id":158618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158104#post158104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you structure Charms? Would each genre have an associated Trait of some kind, something like Astrological Colleges?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily be embracing genres as a hard-coded mechanical thing. The Bard gains power through the stories and how much they mean to him, and given that 3e seems to have Intimacies of ascending importance I think that I'd run with the prerequisite (along with Essence) being the intensity of the Intimacy you've gained towards the story. In retrospect, I can also see the Intimacy being a tie to one of the characters of the story, rather than a lesson or theme gained as a principle. Barring something really resonating with me--and by god I hope something does because right now I can't see a terribly expansive charmset at all--your Investigation charms are going to be things akin to wearing a Deerstalker hat and bearing a magnifying glass because you're a fan of Sherlock Holmes, and taking on some of his capacity like a Resplendent Destiny, or conjuring him whole-cloth into the world that knows he may not be real, but he is *here* and will get to the bottom of this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:39:20-07:00","id":158692,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting!<br /> <br /> I think you still need to divide the charms up *somehow,* if only to keep things better organized and to allow for prerequisites other than bare Essence. <br /> <br /> OOOOH. an idea. Story exalted (hereafter called Taleworkers) have traits similar to Colleges, laid out according to the five elements of a story: plot, character, conflict, setting, and theme. Each charm requires a specific rating in one or more element of story in order to learn, and may have improved effect with a higher rating in an element.<br /> <br /> Plot involves affecting action and change around the Taleworker, along with what little capability the Taleworkers have toward directly achieving their intended goals. A charm which twisted Fate to bring two unknowing allies together would be a Plot/Character charm. If the Elements had associated Virtues, Plot would align with Conviction.<br /> <br /> Character involves directly affecting or modifying the traits of people and living creatures around the Taleworker. A charm which let the Taleworker assume the seductive charm of a great rake from the latest erotic poetry would be a Character/Theme charm. If the Elements had associated Virtues, Character would align with Compassion.<br /> <br /> Conflict involves direct and indirect opposition to another's plans, and also represents most of the Taleworker's combat capabilities. A charm which grants another character an Intimacy directly opposing one of the target's would be a Conflict/Character charm. If the Elements had associated Virtues, Conflict would align with Valor.<br /> <br /> Setting involves directly or indirectly manipulating the world around the Taleworker. A charm which encouraged a fire burning near the Taleworker to spiral out of control, leading to a confrontation amidst a blazing inferno, would be a Setting/Conflict charm. If the Elements had associated Virtues, Setting would align with Temperance.<br /> <br /> Theme is the most subtle element, and involves more indirect manipulation of fate toward a specific idea or condition. Theme also involves meta-story effects, where telling a story has mystical benefits (or detriments) to the listeners. A Charm which penalized friendly interactions in a situation while granting bonuses to aggressive interactions would be a Theme/Conflict charm. If the Elements had associated Virtues, Theme would align with Willpower.<br /> <br /> In addition to granting charm prerequisites, the elements would offer their own bonuses dealing with their bailiwick - somehow. haven't worked out all the bugs. <br /> <br /> In this arrangement, Soul-Sustaining Saga would likely be the opening Theme charm. Sharing Campfire Songs and Life Imitates Art would require low and medium levels of Character, respectively, Heroic Icon Memento would be a Character charm, In Gilded Memories would be Plot/Theme, and Everyone Loves a Story would be Theme/Character. I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T23:06:40-07:00","id":158752,"title":"","content":"A very neat idea! Kudos goes to Mockery! ^__^<br /> <br /> I should really have turned in an hour ago, but eh! I thought I'd add more thoughts to mull over to the small pile of fine suggestions that have already come your way.<br /> <br /> I once babbled on some unorthodox ideas of mine before in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/118248-%E2%80%8Bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation\">here</a>, and think some principles from there may be worth considering, with some other similar notions in a thought experiment from Robert Vance <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/108409-kickstarter-update-59/page27\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> The idea might in this case be to create particular sets of Charms/Evocations/whathaveyou, each geared around a particular story and dependent on maintaining an Intimacy related to it, with higher level effects dependent on a higher level Intimacy (as you'd been thinking). These would be the place to find very particular and distinct effects for those stories -- and may govern the calling of characters, creatures, settings, events, moods, etc. -- and may be where most of the Exalt's power lies. These would presumably be eligible for whatever kinds of xp refund situation Evocations generally see.<br /> <br /> Other Charms might be expressed in a more traditional Ability-/Attribute-/other-based Charmset, defining general story-like powers the Taleweaver can come to command or more... unflavored effects that depend on whatever story is being told and/or whatever stories are close to her heart (e.g. <b>Truth in the Telling</b>, a Socialize/Presence Charm that enhances an Imbue social action to persuade others that all of or some element of a story is true, which works for any old story, but gives greater benefits dependent on the Taleweaver's degree of Intimacy for it). As a side-note, the effect of Soul-Sustaining Saga feels very solid to me, but purchases and repurchases may be a bit much. Perhaps it or some of its effects (the ability to develop Evocations for any stories toward which one holds an Intimacy, for instance) may just be an innate quality of a Taleweaver?<br /> <br /> Another possibility may come from that &quot;Charms as creatures/entities&quot; idea of mine, in which some of the Charms/Evocations/whathaveyou learned for a story can grant a secondary and related effect/use for the Taleweaver, somewhat like the Dreaming/Waking versions for raksha Charms (e.g. created a Charm for Sherlock Holmes? Perhaps the Taleweaver gets a bonus Specialty or extra roll or whatever related to Investigation in a particular context, if not a full-on second Charm).<br /> <br /> There are a couple of other tangential, but still potentially interesting, non-Charm/Evocation angles to consider. One may be thoughts on transference of the Exaltation after death; if you decide such a thing happens, it could be fun and interesting (and edifying) to think about who might generally receive it next. Perhaps one who has come to hold an Intimacy for a story the last Taleweaver cared deeply for -- or even the life story <i>of</i> the last Taleweaver -- might be an especially likely recipient. Perhaps Linguistics Charms could offer some interesting crafting options, allowing a Taleweaver to put beloved stories into books, and subsequently allow other Exalts to develop a bond with a story and call out some Evocations from it. Or even to allow the Taleweaver to revisit the Evocations and other properties of stories for which she may no longer hold an Intimacy (with limits, naturally).<br /> <br /> Also, HobbitGuy, I have no idea if it was intentional, but a number of those work really, really well as ways of describing and thinking about raksha Graces and the general uses thereof. ^_^ I hope you don't mind, but I may need to borrow some of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:37:14-07:00","id":159103,"title":"","content":"I apologize, Hobbitguy, because while you've put forth a lot of ideas with some interesting possibilities, I don't intend to take you up on them here. I'll touch on this below.<br /> <br /> (Also, just because from the way more than one of y'all are talking, I'm going to clarify: I am not envisioning this as a whole new host of Exalted. This is--at least as it's being hammered out in my own mind--a singular entity. Definitely a reincarnating Exaltation, though, because stories do not end.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once babbled on some unorthodox ideas of mine before in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/118248-%E2%80%8Bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation\">here</a>, and think some principles from there may be worth considering, with some other similar notions in a thought experiment from Robert Vance <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/108409-kickstarter-update-59/page27\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're actually pretty on-track with what I was thinking; while I wasn't deliberately channeling TDO's hypothetical Treasurekeeper when I was writing this up, I had definitely read that post before and I'd probably be lying if I said that his potential Exigent wasn't in this one's DNA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea might in this case be to create particular sets of Charms/Evocations/whathaveyou, each geared around a particular story and dependent on maintaining an Intimacy related to it, with higher level effects dependent on a higher level Intimacy (as you'd been thinking). These would be the place to find very particular and distinct effects for those stories -- and may govern the calling of characters, creatures, settings, events, moods, etc. -- and may be where most of the Exalt's power lies. These would presumably be eligible for whatever kinds of xp refund situation Evocations generally see.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually pretty strongly along the lines of what I was thinking. I'm pondering at this point setting the core set like any other story tree, but explicitly based around being the latest in a long line of Talespinner's chosen, and that charms at its core are prerequisites for related charms in the Evocation trees of other stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Charms might be expressed in a more traditional Ability-/Attribute-/other-based Charmset, defining general story-like powers the Taleweaver can come to command or more... unflavored effects that depend on whatever story is being told and/or whatever stories are close to her heart (e.g. <b>Truth in the Telling</b>, a Socialize/Presence Charm that enhances an Imbue social action to persuade others that all of or some element of a story is true, which works for any old story, but gives greater benefits dependent on the Taleweaver's degree of Intimacy for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not 100% sold on this, as I'm not 100% cool with a charmset that restricts itself to a subset of the basis of its charms: While Performance, Presence, Lore, and Linguistics are all really strong candidates for charm trees, and I'm probably overlooking more a couple more, I don't see enough in the way of things like Archery charms, Survival Charms, or Sail Charms--or Strength Charms or Stamina charms or the like--to feel right ascribing this to them in their core set. I would actually feel better placing those kinds of effects in their Evocations.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do like the idea of Truth in the Telling, though.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I'm uncomfortable with wholly new traits just to use your charms, like Hobbitguy was suggesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side-note, the effect of Soul-Sustaining Saga feels very solid to me, but purchases and repurchases may be a bit much. Perhaps it or some of its effects (the ability to develop Evocations for any stories toward which one holds an Intimacy, for instance) may just be an innate quality of a Taleweaver?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd initially rejected the idea of making Soul-Sustaining Saga a non-charm, but the more I think about it, the more I think that's the right way to go. I remember 1e Lunars, which had Finding the Spirit's Shape, a charm that you were more or less required to take (explicitly required if you were Casted). This charm also laid the foundation for a titanic number of Lunar charms, including DBT, Prey's Skin Disguise, and the ones that increased your size range. At that point, it was giving the players a charm slot and mandating that it be spent on this.<br /> <br /> And that's really not fair, as it's tossing you a charm &quot;choice&quot; and then immediately pretty much forcing you to spend it on this one necessary thing.<br /> <br /> It strikes me as poor system design to create something universally necessary, treat it as the gateway to most or all effects, and then make it absolutely mandatory that you have to spend limited, quantifiable amounts of resources on its acquisition to be able to play.<br /> <br /> ...ahem.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Soul-Sustaining Saga is core enough to the powerset and low-grade enough in power that in retrospect I can only see how making its effects a hard-coded aspect of the Exaltation to be a good thing, possibly with a Merit to reflect how many stories you possess rather than charm repurchases here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple of other tangential, but still potentially interesting, non-Charm/Evocation angles to consider. One may be thoughts on transference of the Exaltation after death; if you decide such a thing happens, it could be fun and interesting (and edifying) to think about who might generally receive it next. Perhaps one who has come to hold an Intimacy for a story the last Taleweaver cared deeply for -- or even the life story <i>of</i> the last Taleweaver -- might be an especially likely recipient.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, I have definitely considered. The heir to the Exigent's Exaltation is usually someone who's been touched by Sharing Campfire Songs. Talespinner--or whoever the patron is--doesn't seem to have much control over it regardless. The Exaltation comes to its future bearer wearing the face of its previous one, for one last story. It takes place in a day and an eyeblink at once, but it's the story of all the new Exalt's predecessors. I imagine it lays the groundwork for something like the 1e Lunar Intelligence charm Lore-Speaking Method, aka &quot;I remember everything ever, with a little rooting around.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Linguistics Charms could offer some interesting crafting options, allowing a Taleweaver to put beloved stories into books, and subsequently allow other Exalts to develop a bond with a story and call out some Evocations from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see book-evocations as working right. This Exigent I strongly imagine as a verbal teller of tales--he probably reads to glean information, but he doesn't necessarily jot it down later. I can see it, however, as an extension of something like Heroic Icon Memento...<br /> <br /> &quot;...look! Look at this!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This is the sky-plumage of Araz Ku. What a treasure! Do you know--&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's a feather from a bluejay's wing. I just saw it fall. YOU saw it fall--&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Pff. Of course you'd think that, child. I understand. But you haven't heard, I suppose...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not ag--&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;For once when he was young, Araz Ku was a prince in his garden...&quot;<br /> <br /> &lt;Two hours later&gt;<br /> <br /> &quot;And so to this day he beats his wings tirelessly, invisibly, but sometimes a single one of his feathers falls, like so. And usually nature takes it, or some foolish dandy sticks it in their hat until it's ratty and done, and it does nothing then. But I suspect--just between you and me--that just as his road to the heavens began with a single feather, you or I might follow with this one. But what do I know, it's just a story. Still...here, take it with you. Perhaps it will bear you up to the clouds with time, as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/157997-rough-idea-for-an-exigent-the-chosen-of-stories?p=158752#post158752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or even to allow the Taleweaver to revisit the Evocations and other properties of stories for which she may no longer hold an Intimacy (with limits, naturally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd been toying with the idea of a charm--after a few stories had been delved into--that gave this Exalt a more generalized intimacy that could support countless stories on a lower level indefinitely. He can channel the stories he truly loves to their utmost, but aren't all of them really worthwhile to some degree? I'm also kicking around the idea of a charm that lets you try a story out--temporarily get access to some of the lower charms and respective evocations without absorbing it in a meaningful manner.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 06-04-2014, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:45:33-07:00","id":159150,"title":"","content":"Before you do much else, I would recommend that you set down the thesis of the splat. That is, what are they meant to accomplish in a narrative sense, and how do they compare and contrast with the Solar Exalted and the other Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:53:55-07:00","id":174237,"title":"","content":"Okay, it's been like two weeks since I was asked this question, and I'm still having a little trouble on it. But for starters, this Exalt--again, not a splat, just a single man or woman--generally acts in one of two or three roles:<br /> <br /> On their own, they're generally a subtle influence, seeking out unfamiliar stories and sometimes being around to witness--and occasionally kick off--the formation of new ones. In the latter case, the locals are usually aware of the Exigent's presence--he's rarely subtle--though not what it signifies nor of the change that he inevitably heralds. In a group of other Exalted, he's a capable support person, one of the best PR men you can ask for, and like any Exalt probably capable of surviving a tough scrape better than 99% of Creation. But he's better suited to letting the others take center stage against larger threats--especially those that refuse to be put away with anything less heavy or drastic than the razor-honed edge of a daiklave.<br /> <br /> In other words, he's a hero (his powers lend themselves quite well to a Guile Hero), but almost never <i>the</i> hero.<br /> <br /> There's some definite Sidereal in his conceptual DNA, combined with lore-heavy adventuring Twilight and a smattering of Mirror Flag. But given that it's a single entity with some unique and defining tricks, I'm not too concerned with the possibility that I could adapt this to another splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}